    "Apex response has no x-robots-tag: noindex header. SEO counts toward the verdict this run. All 6 URLs score SEO 100. The prior SEO 69 was the staging noindex artifact.",
    "Lighthouse ran DESKTOP only (for_mobile=false; the DataForSEO wrapper exposes no form_factor). Mobile scores would typically run 10-20 performance points lower, and the 1.42 MB logo.png would hurt far more on mobile.",
    "Service-landing slots: fire-damage-restoration, mold-remediation and water-damage-restoration all have url-plan priority 9.0. Kept water-damage-restoration and fire-damage-restoration (the 2026-08-26 selection) so the regression comparison stays valid.",
    "Service-area slot: url-plan has no primary:true entry and the client record has no business.address.city. Used /service-areas/warren-oh/ (first area slug, same as prior run).",
    "DataForSEO instant_pages returned has_micromarkup=null on all 6 URLs. Verified directly against the served HTML: home ships Organization, WebSite, LocalBusiness; hub and contact add FAQPage, BreadcrumbList; service landings ship Service, LocalBusiness, FAQPage, BreadcrumbList; service area ships LocalBusiness, FAQPage, BreadcrumbList. The only schema gap is FAQPage on the homepage.",
    "Apex HTML now loads Google Analytics 4 (gtag.js G-QQDEBB808D), Google Fonts (Inter), and Cloudflare email-decode.min.js (Email Obfuscation). None were on the staging baseline, which contributes to the performance deltas.",
    "Lighthouse lantern-simulated LCP is about 1.9-2.0 s on every page even though observed LCP subparts total about 300-400 ms. The simulated number is dominated by the 2.1-2.4 MB page weight (1.42 MB of it is logo.png) competing for bandwidth at the 10 Mbps throttle.",
    "lighthouse_issues is capped at 5 per URL. lighthouse_failing_audit_ids lists every failing audit (score < 0.9) so future runs can do full new/resolved diffs."
